Ansible Interview Questions 🎯

🔹 PHASE 6: Projects & Interview Prep
Today I focused on Ansible Interview Preparation, covering real-world scenarios and DevOps-focused questions 💼
Understanding concepts is important — but being able to explain them clearly in interviews is even more important 🚀

🔹 🌍 Real-World Scenarios
Interviewers often ask scenario-based questions like:
• How would you deploy an application using Ansible?
 • How do you handle different configurations for dev and prod?
 • How do you restart services only when configs change?
 • How do you manage secrets securely?
These questions test practical understanding, not just theory.

🔹 ⚙️ DevOps-Focused Q&A
Common technical areas covered:
✔ Difference between Ad-Hoc and Playbooks
 ✔ How idempotency works
 ✔ Variable precedence
 ✔ Roles and directory structure
 ✔ Error handling (block, rescue, always)
 ✔ CI/CD integration
Interview focus is usually on automation design thinking 🧠

🔹 ⚠️ Common Mistakes
Many candidates make mistakes like:
• Not explaining idempotency clearly
 • Ignoring security practices (Vault)
 • Confusing host_vars and group_vars
 • Not knowing how to debug failures
 • Giving only theoretical answers
Clear, structured answers make a strong impression 💪

🔥 3-Line Takeaway
Interviews test practical automation thinking.
 Understand concepts, not just syntax.
 Confidence + clarity = strong DevOps interviews.
